    "durationMs": 153094,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and verified — 55/55 checks pass, including a restart persistence test.\n\n**What I built** (Express 4.21 + Knex over PostgreSQL, all deps installed locally):\n- `src/app.js` — routes: `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, generated or custom codes), `GET /links/:code`, `GET /r/:code` (atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` then 302 redirect), `GET /links` (ascending order, `{items, total}`). Errors are always JSON: 409 duplicate custom code, 404 unknown code/route, 422 for malformed JSON, invalid/missing url, and invalid codes.\n- `migrations/20261122000000_create_links.js` — `links` table (`code` unique, `url`, `clicks` default 0, `created_at`), applied via `knex migrate:latest`.\n- `start.sh` — validates `DATABASE_URL`, applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (no installs inside).\n- `README.md` — start instructions plus API reference.\n\n**Notable fix found during testing:** Node's WHATWG URL parser accepts `https:///nohost` by skipping the extra slashes, so I added a raw-string check requiring a non-empty host right after `scheme://` — that case now correctly returns 422.\n\nVerified across a full stop/start cycle: all links and click counts survived, and migrations were a no-op on restart. The test server has been stopped; port 8000 is free."
  }
